  "amendments": [
    {
      "version": 2,
      "reason": "Every selective protocol-1 lesion that preserved non-target behavior was undone by refitting the full last layer on the diagnostic set. The grammatical label was still linearly decodable from the second hidden layer, so those lesions were readout problems. Protocol 2 adds a gender-column copy in fc1: the input weight for gender_neuter is replaced by the weight for gender_uter. A neuter phrase then has the same hidden state as its uter counterpart. Plural and definite exponents already ignore gender, so those cells stay correct, while singular indefinite neuter forms are predicted as the uter base. A later linear layer cannot assign two labels to one hidden state. The target set is this strong-neuter cell across lexical classes, not the geminating subclass alone."
    }
  ],
